---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How it works"
  description="Anchor uses spaced retrieval in the family Telegram group so Athina can practise remembering — gently, on her own schedule."
  currentPath="/how-it-works"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>How it works</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Anchor lives in the Telegram group the family already uses. No new app. No training sessions. Just memories coming
      back at the right time.
    </p>

    <h2>Family shares a moment</h2>
    <p>
      Someone drops a photo, a voice note, or a short line into the family group — Maria's first day of school, Sunday
      lunch, a walk by the sea. Anchor saves it as a practiceable memory.
    </p>

    <h2>Spaced retrieval</h2>
    <p>
      Later, Anchor brings the moment back with a gentle question that does not give the answer away. Remembering freely
      stretches the wait. A cue holds the schedule. A struggle resets to tomorrow.
    </p>

    <h2>She stays in the story</h2>
    <p>
      The family keeps talking. Athina keeps her place in it — not as a patient of a new tool, but as grandmother in the
      same chat.
    </p>

    <h2>Website</h2>
    <p>
      Registration starts with your email, so you can read the privacy policy. Then you add Anchor to the family group,
      create the family, and upload a memory. Choices and admin tools stay in Telegram.
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top: 2rem; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/family">Get started</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/app">Try the scripted demo</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
